---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About"
			description="Quick bio and background for Felix van Doorn."
		/>
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
				margin: auto;
				padding: 3em 1em;
			}
			section {
				margin-top: 2.5em;
			}
			ul {
				padding-left: 1.2em;
			}
			li {
				margin-bottom: 0.75em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p>
				I'm Felix, a data-obsessed product builder with a bit of a polymath streak. I've spent
				most of my career working in data at Big Tech companies, and outside of work you'll find
				me writing (for my golf club's magazine, and now here) or out on the course with an out
				of control golf hobby.
			</p>

			<section>
				<h2>What I've done</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Product Analyst I</strong>, Uber (2019–2022) — built payment experience and financial products</li>
					<li><strong>Data Scientist II</strong>, Uber (2022–2024) — earnings data platform, driver app experience and regulatory benefits</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>What I'm doing</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Sr Analytics Engineer</strong>, Netflix — promotional media for on-service, marketing and social teams</li>
					<li>Writing essays and technical breakdowns on this blog</li>
					<li>Building an MVP with the team at Helyx Energy</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Where I want to go</h2>
				<p>
					My key area of interest is how we can apply the latest advances in Data/ML/AI to the
					core systems delivering value and utility to society, such as finance, energy grids,
					construction, agriculture and pharma. I want to contribute to these areas as more of a
					"full-stack builder", blending elements of engineering, science, product management and
					investing to find what to build and build it.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
